1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
You didn't run over anything.

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:05,000
That warning light isn't damage —
it's the weather.

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Every ten degrees the temperature drops
pulls about one PSI out of every tire.

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:15,000
That's why the light shows up on the first
cold Cleveland morning — out of nowhere.

5
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Warm tires read high
and hide the real number.

6
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:25,000
Check the pressure cold, before you drive —
that's the number that counts.

7
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Worth checking before that first frost.
